            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0573" n="537" xml:id="pg537"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3943a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-27T14:00:00-05:00">March 27, 1919—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7853. Department’s 7549, February 27th. Your attention is called to the fact that
                    no reports whatever on the general attitude of the French press have been
                    received for the past ten days. Department requests that it be kept more fully
                    advised on this subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
